@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. The browser surfaces are the `entity.queues` page (`App\Livewire\Entity\Queues`, owner/admin: create, rename with slug re-derived from the name, deactivate/reactivate behind a confirmation modal, per-queue `call` grants) and the `entity.serve` panel (`App\Livewire\Entity\Serve`, any member: callable queues, waiting list capped at 30, mode selector, `callNext()` rate-limited to 10 successful calls/min per user and entity). Both call the domain actions and resolve every client-sent id scoped to the current entity.
 
 ### Priority
 
@@ -134,6 +134,8 @@ ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
 After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
 
+The web panel (`entity.serve`) exposes the mode as a selector (`any`, `priority_only`, `normal_only`) plus a single **Call next** button; there is no separate button per mode.
+
